<title>AUSTRALIA: BHP to book A$45mln loss on Mali sale.</title>
<headline>BHP to book A$45mln loss on Mali sale.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd said on Wednesday that it sold its gold mining interests in Mali, West Africa, at A$45 million below book value and this would be reflected in its August quarter results.  </p>
<p>&quot;The transaction price is approximately A$45 million below BHP's book value for its interests in Mali,&quot; BHP said.</p>
<p>&quot;This will be reflected in the August quarterly results.&quot;</p>
<p>The sale, to South Africa's Rangold Resources, covered 65 percent of the Syama gold mine and exploration interests in Mali, BHP said.</p>
<p>&quot;BHP retains its interest in developing quality gold projects when opportunities occur, however the nature of the medium-sized operations in Mali no longer fit BHP Minerals' strategies for growth,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne Bureau 613-9286-1421</p>
